Spark: New Year, New Look!=20
Wellness UpdateBy Julie Paris
January 2026, you're getting a new and updated Akamai Spark employee engage=
ment experience; with even greater integration, ease of use, and loads of in=
credible content. Participate in this campaign to learn more about the new e=
xperience. See you on Spark!

READ MORE =C2=BB=20
  =20
 DLCCD in MilanInternal and External EventsBy Chiara Molinari
At the end of October, our colleagues in Milan hosted their annual DLCCD ev=
ent in support of Humana, a nonprofit that collects and redistributes used c=
lothing to promote social and environmental impact. The team gathered and do=
nated an impressive amount of clothes. It was so nice to see everyone workin=
g together and contributing their energy and enthusiasm for such a great pur=
pose.
READ MORE =C2=BB My Vision of Akamai in 2030Internal and External EventsBy Kari=
ne Gourdon-Keller, Johannes FordemannSenior members of the German team came =
together in the Munich office for an engaging panel discussion on =E2=80=9CMy Visi=
on of Akamai in 2030.=E2=80=9D The conversation sparked great energy as leaders ex=
plored how AI, platformization, and a more agile way of working will shape o=
ur path forward.
READ MORE =C2=BB=20
  =20
 EMEA Town Hall November - recording available!Internal and External Events
Our EMEA Town Hall on 19th November 2025 brought the region together for bu=
siness updates, a panel on Cloud & AI, and the Year in Review. If you weren=E2=
=80=99t able to join, the recording is now available to watch. You can also watc=
h the EMEA Year in Review video. We look forward to connecting with you agai=
n next year on another Town Hall!
READ MORE =C2=BB EMEA & Poland ID&E - Neurodiversity Employee PanelInternal and=
 External EventsBy Hamish RoseAkamai=E2=80=99s EMEA and Poland ID&E teams, with Kh=
alil Smith, VP of Inclusion, Diversity & Engagement, hosted a session with n=
eurodivergent colleagues and a parent of neurodivergent children sharing the=
ir experiences. They discussed the challenges and strengths of neurodivergen=
ce and offered practical tips for fostering an inclusive culture. The record=
ing is now available - definitely worth a watch to gain insights on supporti=
ng an inclusive workplace.
READ MORE =C2=BB=20
    =20
  =20
Akamai Spain Takes 2nd Place at Great Place to Work Awards! Spotlight
We=E2=80=99re excited to share some fantastic news: at yesterday=E2=80=99s Great Place =
to Work awards ceremony, Akamai Spain was recognized as the second-best comp=
any in the country for organizations with up to 100 employees - a great high=
 placement! This recognition highlights our strong culture of collaboration,=
 respect, and growth across the region. Congratulations to everyone for maki=
ng this possible!
